<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 0.72 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 0.72 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.2955 to the dollar on Friday, up from 3.2990 on Thursday and at 1.8800 to the mark, up from 1.8810, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 0.72 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Thursday's 0.69 percent fix.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
